Sval: per-site, per-session navigator.hardwareConcurrency

A new RFPTarget, NavigatorHWConcurrencyRandomized, makes
navigator.hardwareConcurrency a count in [max(2, ceil(real / 2)), real]. A
fixed count is the same on every site and across restarts, so it is a stable
identifier; a drawn one links no two sites, and a web app sizing a worker
pool to it keeps at least half its parallelism.

SvalRFPService::RandomizedHardwareConcurrency draws the count from the
fingerprinting randomization key canvas and audio noise use: the key
cookieJarSettings carries, derived from the browsing session key and the
top-level site, so it is fixed for a site within a session, and private
browsing has its own. RuntimeService::ClampedHardwareConcurrency answers
documents and workers alike, each from its own global's key. A dedicated
worker shares its document's cookieJarSettings, a shared worker's is
serialized from it, and a service worker's comes from
GenerateKeyForServiceWorker's derivation of the same key, so every realm of
a site reads one count. RFP's fixed NavigatorHWConcurrency takes precedence
over it, and it over the tiers. The key is made when any randomization
target is on, so this one joins kRandomizationTargets, which
GetBrowsingSessionKey and GenerateKey check. RandomizationDigest is the HMAC
both this and AudioOutputNoiseKey draw from, each under its own target's
name. The target is Doc-gated, so a site's -AllTargets granular entry gives
it the real count.

No chrome API can change what navigator.hardwareConcurrency returns.

